Z||000013||falconhulk||10-09-2001||09:11 AM||||the 1.8 is a 4cy not a 6cy.  You would definitely smoke an 83 jetta with a v6 fiero and probably a 4cy, the new 4cy jetta turbos put out 185 Hp.  From early 90's to recently it was 145 HP.  Not sure of a number but back in 83 it was MUCH less.  Remember back then the Fiero was FAST!<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||DreXteR||10-09-2001||10:11 AM||||If the jetta is 4 cl and dont have any mod you can take him. Do this, ake the air filter off for the race, buy a bottle of octane booster and use 93 fuel-half tank- <B>this is before the race</B>. The week before use injector cleaner or a sort of thing, make a full tune up. Check the engine time. Take the spare tire off an the stuff dont needed. This is for one race only, then you put all back in place.<P>Anithing besides that will be spend money, the tune up is good for the car plus the octane booster is cheaper. <P>Go for it, if you win laugh @ him, if you loose be friendly and ask him what he got in there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   Tha good attitud of a racer.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000015||falconhulk||10-09-2001||12:16 PM||||exactly why would he need an octane booster?  Is his engine prone to detonation?  Did I miss something?  Unless he is losing power due to early detonation octane booster will not help a bit.  It might help clean the injection system since it has a few more detergent agents.||||reg||1
Z||000016||DreXteR||10-09-2001||03:43 PM||||Well why to use 93 instead of 86!  The same goes for octane booster, ITS NO NOS but will help.<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000017||falconhulk||10-09-2001||03:54 PM||||I think you are confused.  NOS works becasue it releases a lot of oxygen real fast.  You then combine more fuel with that o2 to create more power.  Octane only adds power by creating a harder to ignite mixture.  What this does it make detonation (ignition due to heat and not spark) less likely.  Detonation robs the engine of power and also damages the engine.  A stock 4 cyl fiero that does not suffer from problems will not have detonantion.  if it does running higher octane gas will just prolong the time you can ignore the problem.  Also to much octane can make the mixture take to long to ignite and rob you of power also.  Even the 6cy normally aspirated engine should not need to run anything over premium.  If you have a super or turbocharger running a good amount of boost without a intercooler then yes you need it.  Even with an intercooler at higher boosts octane booster is required. <p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
